          "pantryKey": "sour-cream"
        }
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Cut beef across grain into about 1\u00bd x \u00bd inch strips. (Beef is easier to cut if partially frozen, about 1 hour.)",
        "Melt margarine in 10-inch skillet over medium-high heat. Cook beef in margarine, stirring occasionally, until brown.",
        "Reserve \u2153 cup of the broth. Stir remaining broth, the ketchup, salt and garlic into skillet. Heat to boiling; reduce heat to low. Cover and simmer about 10 minutes or until beef is tender.",
        "Stir in mushrooms and onion. Cover and simmer about 5 minutes or until onion is tender.",
        "Shake reserved broth and the flour in tightly covered container; gradually stir into beef mixture. Heat to boiling, stirring constantly. Boil and stir 1 minute; reduce heat to low.",
        "Stir in sour cream; cook until hot. Serve over noodles."
      ],
      "notes": "Quickest of the three stroganoff versions. 300 cal per serving. Lighter version: decrease margarine to 1 tbsp, use nonstick skillet and reduced-fat sour cream/yogurt for 265 cal."
